{
  "case_id": "2016-15-214",
  "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Let me ask you this question. It's a hypothetical. It's not this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Groen, may I ask --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in case 15-214, Murr v. Wisconsin."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John M. Groen",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GROEN: They should pay for -- compensation for the taking of Lot E. Any taking --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask a question? I do think, as I'm reading all of the briefs in this case, that the issue is how much weight should we be giving to the State boundary lines, the State property lines."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Groen",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "begin the analysis by identifying the relevant parcel. Here, that has to be Lot E. It was purchased separately. It's a separate deed. It was purchased for separate purposes, and it is the lot that is regulated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me give you -- let me give you an example which might help me. Let's go back to Holmes case. There's a hundred acres. There are 50 columns of coal to hold up the -- to hold up the ceiling. That he says is okay. No compensation. But wait. Suppose instead of one people -- one person owning all 50 acres, suppose 50 people each own one acre. And in some cases, the column runs through the acre and some it doesn't. Does that make any difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Tseyltin",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The lots here have merged for all relevant purposes under State law. It is true that the lot line between Lot E and Lot F still exists, but that has absolutely no continuing legal relevance under State law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Would interpret it what way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. TSEYTLIN: Well, let me explain what the State is trying to achieve in this law. It wants to ultimately phase out substandard lots in the long term. It does not want to interfere with any current investment-backed expectations. So what it says is we're going to have a slow phaseout and it's going to be only triggered by the situation where people end up taking the lots in common ownership. And that will happen in the long term."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "St. Croix County",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The value of the two parcels together for one house is $698,000. The value of two houses separate, with a house on each, is $771,000."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry. I've had a problem with the appraisal figures, and it may be a step I'm missing. Why would anybody pay $400,000 for a lot they can't build on?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (counsel MR. LAZARUS)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LAZARUS: Well, the question is not the -- what the value of Lot E as a unit that you can't develop or -- or build on. The question is what the value of Lot E is to the Murrs, who also own Lot F, because that's how you define what the burden is to them. And the burden to them -- if -- if someone only owned Lot E, then the hardship exemption would apply and they could build. That's exactly the distinction that the ordinance draws between the two."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is this right? Just say yes or no, and if it's wrong, I'll figure it out later."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Temporal considerations. Now, you usually don't say that when you're asking about property. You say, I owned Lot E or I own Lot F, and here it is on the map; that's what I own."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e3ac643b4d24b9996ec7ddd760b7c5366b461a4289656420bee36d7c522ebf4f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e3ac643b4d24-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: The problem I have with your test, which has the -- the three components, is I don't actually see anywhere in there any weight given to the State property lines."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-214",
      "confidence": 0.0,
